FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin","name":"Antonia Bossin","dates":"10 Jan 1849 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 1894","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"10 Jan 1849 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1849-01-10","died":"1894","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"guilielmus_bossin","mother":"peremans","spouses":[{"id":"georges_cj","name":"Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas","detail":"20 Jun 1872 (Kraainem)"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872","note":"SPELLING CORRECTED (July 2026): *Antonia*, not \"Antoina\". the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]) names her as the\nbridegroom's mother, which is also what fixes her as the mother of [[jbgeorgius]]. The act\ngives her no dates and no occupation, so none is recorded — her own birth and marriage\nacts are the frontier.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by her own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872 — which names\nher as the bride, born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and gives **both her parents**:\nGuilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina Peremans. The tree already had [[guilielmus_bossin]]\nand [[peremans]] as her parents on a member tree's word; the act settles it.\n\nHer mother is written *Anna* Catharina Peremans here, where this tree calls her Joanna\nCatharina Jacoba. Both forms are recorded, and neither is preferred without a second act.\n\nACT READ (July 2026). The Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 has now been read on\nAGATHA rather than through an index, and it sharpens this record twice: her birth is\n**10 January 1849** where the tree had only the year, at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, and her\ntrade at marriage was *fabriekwerkster*. Her parents are named in the act."});
