FamilyTree.person({"id":"elisabeth_nn","name":"Elisabeth NN","dates":"","confidence":"sup","sex":"f","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"livinus_bundervoet","name":"Livinus Bundervoet","detail":"1st — mother of Segerius"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"First wife of Livinus Bundervoet and mother of Segerius Bundervoet (~1615–1669), so a\ndirect ancestor. Her given name is all that survives: the paulderidder tree records her\nas \"Elisabeth NN\", with no surname, no dates and no parents.\n\nSURNAME NOT KNOWN — and specifically not \"Hovelynck\". Livinus's record here used to\ncall her Elisabeth Hovelynck; the paulderidder tree, which that claim was attributed\nto, gives no surname at all. The surname has been removed rather than carried forward,\nbecause a name that no reachable source states is exactly the kind of detail that\nhardens into fact by being repeated. If another tree does give a surname, it can be\nrestored with that tree cited.\n\nFRONTIER: an Evergem marriage of Livinus Bundervoet in the 1610s would name her in\nfull, and would also settle which of his two marriages came first."});
