FamilyTree.person({"id":"jbgeorgius","name":"Joannes Baptista Georgius Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem – 23 Mar 1944 Brussel","confidence":"doc","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem","order":"1876-09-26","died":"23 Mar 1944 Brussel","occupation":"fabriekwerker & gemeenteschepen (factory worker & alderman)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges_cj","mother":"bossin","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbemden","name":"Joanna Vandenbemden","detail":"Kraainem, 3 Feb 1902"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; marcelcroon (Marcel Croon); jswaelens","note":"Son of Georges Carolus Josephus and Antoina Bossin. A factory worker who also served as a schepen (municipal alderman) in Kraainem. Married Joanna Vandenbemden in Kraainem on 3 Feb 1902.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where he is the bridegroom. It gives his birth at\nKraainem on 26 September 1876 and his trade as *fabriekwerker*, both as held here, and\nnames his parents outright — Georgius Carolus Josephus Thumas and Antonia Bossin. He was\nliving at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe when he married. The alderman's office in his occupation\nfield came from elsewhere and is not in this act."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jean_t","name":"Jean Thumas","dates":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem – 22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem","order":"1907-10-23","died":"22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jbgeorgius","mother":"vandenbemden","spouses":[{"id":"crabbe","name":"Marie Louise Crabbé"}],"note":"DOCUMENTED (b. 23 Oct 1907, d. 22 Mar 1995, both in Kraainem; Geneanet, marcelcroon). He lived his whole life in Kraainem and is the strongly-supported grandfather of Thiery. The ONE remaining sealed link is Jean → François (Thiery’s father), whose 20th-century birth is behind the 100-year civil-registration privacy wall."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jeanlambert_t","name":"Jean Lambert Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau – 3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"doc","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1701-09-26","died":"3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"marguillier & greffier (church warden / parish clerk)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"antoine_t","mother":"daix","spouses":[{"id":"leclercq_t","name":"Marie Jacqueline Leclercq","detail":"Wavre, 23 Feb 1743 — his 2nd marriage"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father. His son Georges's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20\nNovember 1808) names the dead man's father as *Lambert Thumas* and his mother as Marie\nLeclercq — the pairing this record already asserts, now on a civil act rather than on the\nm2155 tree alone. The act gives the short form of his name, without the *Jean*.\n\nChurch warden and parish clerk of Grez-Doiceau. Our line descends from his SECOND marriage, to Marie Jacqueline Leclercq (Wavre, 1743) — their son Georges (1744) continues the line. His first wife was Marie Catherine Crèvecœur (m. 1727, d. 1742).\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as *Lambert Thumas of Grez*, father of the deceased, in his son\nGeorge's 1808 Grez-Doiceau death act — with [[leclercq_t]] as the mother. The couple and the\nparentage are now on a civil act."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jeanne_deconninck","name":"Jeanne Marie Deconninck","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Deconninck","family":"deconninck","sex":"f","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"guillaume_joostens","name":"Guillaume Joostens"}],"source":"Death act nr. 35 — Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857 (read on AGATHA); Death act of Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857","note":"Mother of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857) and so a direct ancestor.\n\nNamed alongside her husband in her daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857, which\nis the only source read for her. It gives her no dates and no place; none is invented here.\n\nThe surname is Flemish (De Coninck / Deconinck are the commoner spellings) in a\nWalloon-Brabant setting, which is worth noting for the search: the family may have come to\nWoluwe-Saint-Lambert or Grez-Doiceau from Flanders, and the name may be spelled either way\nin the registers.\n\nFRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and her own parents.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the mother of the deceased in her daughter's 1857\nGrez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. As with her husband, the act gives her nothing\nbeyond the name."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jerome_dk","name":"Jerome Joseph Dekeyser","dates":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende – 1972 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende","order":"1897-06-14","died":"1972 Oostende","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","father":"edouard_dk","mother":"louise_bocklandt","spouses":[{"id":"leonie_p","name":"Léonie (Philomena Leonia) Paelinck","detail":"10 Dec 1919, Sint-Niklaas"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck); Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Oostende Burgerzaken; Rijksarchief AGATHA (Oostende birth act nr. 585, 1897)\n\nCONFIRMED Roland's grandfather (Cosette). Full first names Jérôme Josephus; born Oostende 14 Jun 1897 (birth act nr. 585, Rijksarchief AGATHA). Born before his parents married: he was LEGITIMIZED by their marriage on 4 May 1901 (marginal note 'Gewettigd 4 5 1901' on his birth act). Lived in Oostende (Blauwkasteelstraat 21; later Amsterdamstraat 38). Recorded child: Albert Dekeyser (1920–1972); Gustaaf (Roland's father) is another of their sons. His siblings (children of Édouard × Louise, per AGATHA): Gustavus Josephus (1899, also legitimized 1901), Bertha Alida Theresia (1901), Maria (1902–2002), Angela Luciana (†1903) and Cesar Mauritius (†1905) — the last two died in infancy."});
