FamilyTree.person({"id":"leclercq_t","name":"Marie Jacqueline Leclercq","dates":"30 Oct 1710 Grez-Doiceau – 14 Apr 1786 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"doc","surname":"Leclercq","family":"leclercq","born":"30 Oct 1710 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1710-10-30","died":"14 Apr 1786 Grez-Doiceau","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"jeanlambert_t","name":"Jean Lambert Thumas","detail":"Wavre, 23 Feb 1743"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a mother. Her son Georges's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20\nNovember 1808) names his mother as *Marie Leclercq*, alongside the father Lambert Thumas —\nwhich puts this couple, and her motherhood of the line's Georges, on a civil act.\n\nSecond wife of Jean Lambert Thumas (m. Wavre 1743) and mother of the line's Georges (1744); the couple had eight children.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as *Marie Leclercq of Grez*, mother of the deceased, in her son\nGeorge's 1808 Grez-Doiceau death act, beside the father Lambert Thumas."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"leon","name":"Léon Bundervoet","dates":"b. 9 Aug 2019 Leuven","confidence":"fam","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"m","born":"9 Aug 2019 Leuven","order":"2019-08-09","line":"immediate","father":"shaun","mother":"dorien","note":"Born in Leuven, 9 August 2019 — the younger of the two youngest, and Renée's brother. He and Renée are what this tree was built for. The two of them were previously held in a single entry, \"Renée & Léon Bundervoet\"; split apart so each has their own dates."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"leonie_p","name":"Léonie (Philomena Leonia) Paelinck","dates":"31 Oct 1901 Sint-Niklaas – 1992","confidence":"doc","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"31 Oct 1901 Sint-Niklaas","order":"1901-10-31","died":"1992","nickname":"Meme Lenie","branch":"Paelinck","line":"de-keyser","father":"eduardus_p","mother":"magdalena_vb","spouses":[{"id":"jerome_dk","name":"Jerome Joseph Dekeyser","detail":"10 Dec 1919, Sint-Niklaas"}],"source":"Birth registration nr. 997 — Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; Birth act of Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Sint-Niklaas marriage 1919\n\nFrom Sint-Niklaas — she opens the deep Paelinck line, documented to ~1618.\n\nDOCUMENTED DATE (July 2026). Her birth act — Sint-Niklaas, **31 October 1901** — gives\nthe day the tree had only as a year, and names both parents in the act itself:\n[[eduardus_p]] and [[magdalena_vb]]. Those two links stood on the stefpaelinck tree\nuntil now.\n\nFOUND ON FAMILYSEARCH (July 2026), after AGATHA had been recorded as a NOT FOUND for this\nsame act. Her birth registration — Sint-Niklaas, **31 October 1901**, invoernummer **997** —\nis indexed in *Belgium, East Flanders, Civil Registration, 1541-1950*, with both parents\nattached: [[eduardus_p]] and [[magdalena_vb]] ([[S16]]).\n\nThe correction to make here is not to the record but to how it was searched. AGATHA holds\neight Paelinck entries for Sint-Niklaas and no births, and that was written up as though the\nact did not exist. It exists; one archive did not have it.\n\nREGISTER PAGE READ (July 2026). Not the index card this time but the act itself —\nSint-Niklaas births 1901, image 268, act nr. 997 ([[leonie-paelinck-1901-birth-register]]).\nHer names are written out at the close of the act as *Philomena Leonia*, with her father and\nmother named in the body. Confidence raised to `doc` on that reading."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"leontius_v","name":"Leontius Ivo Vanstechelman","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"m","branch":"Vanstechelman","line":"vanstechelman","father":"petrusjacobus_v","mother":"clementia_w","spouses":[{"name":"Lucia Amelia Maene","detail":"Oostende, 20 Aug 1922"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Brother of [[augusta]], named in his own Oostende marriage registration of 20 August 1922,\nwhich gives his parents as Petrus Jacobus and Clementia Sophia Wagebaert and his bride as\nLucia Amelia Maene.\n\nNo dates of his own: the marriage act is indexed under the event, not his birth, and nothing\nelse has been read for him. FRONTIER — his birth act at Mariakerke or Oostende would give\nthem, and the marriage act itself, read rather than indexed, would give both spouses' ages\nand his wife's parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livina_dewilde","name":"Livina De Wilde","dates":"d. 1750 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Wilde","family":"dewilde","sex":"f","died":"1750 Evergem","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"joannes_b","name":"Joannes Bundervoet","detail":"~1745 — his 2nd wife"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Joannes Bundervoet's SECOND wife (married ~1745, died 1750) — NOT the mother of\nChristoffel or Pieter; both were by his first wife, Livina Stockman. Several trees\nconfuse the two wives.\n\nGIVEN NAME DISPUTED. This record calls her Livina; the paulderidder tree calls her\n**Joanna de Wilde**, and gives her no dates at all — the 1750 death here comes from\nglorieuxp. Both trees are cited below, and they do not agree, so the name is held\nloosely: \"Livina\" is what this record has always said and is kept for stability, but it\nis not settled. The confusion is easy to see how it started, since the first wife was\nalso a Livina. FRONTIER: the ~1745 Evergem marriage act would name her outright and\nsettle it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livina_pickaut","name":"Livina Pickaut","dates":"17 Feb 1687 Lochristi – 22 Nov 1726 Lochristi","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pickaut","family":"pickaut","born":"17 Feb 1687 Lochristi","order":"1687-02-17","died":"22 Nov 1726 Lochristi","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"adrianus_p","name":"Adrianus Paelinck","detail":"Lochristi, 17 Jan 1711"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Died in 1726, the same year as her husband Adrianus; mother of Livinus (1718)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livina_stockman","name":"Livina Stockman","dates":"~1688 – 1744 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stockman","family":"stockman","born":"~1688","order":"1688","died":"1744 Evergem","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"joannes_stockman","mother":"guillielma_dellaert","spouses":[{"id":"joannes_b","name":"Joannes Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Source detail: Geneanet trees glorieuxp & paulderidder (both give her as c.1688-1744)\n\nJoannes Bundervoet's FIRST wife and mother of Christoffel (1709) and Pieter (1727). She died in 1744; Joannes then remarried Livina (Joanna) De Wilde ~1745 — the remarriage confirmed independently by the glorieuxp and paulderidder trees, and consistent with the chronology (Christoffel's 1709 birth predates the De Wilde marriage). Several other trees wrongly list Christoffel's mother as De Wilde."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livinus1_p","name":"Livinus Paelinck","dates":"b. ~1618 Lochristi","confidence":"sup","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"~1618 Lochristi","order":"1618","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"elisabeth_t","name":"Elisabeth Temmerman","detail":"Gent, 18 Jan 1645"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Earliest documented Paelinck ancestor; the family was rooted in Lochristi (Oost-Vlaanderen). Married Elisabeth Temmerman at Gent in 1645 (the old '1645' was his marriage year, not a death date)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livinus2_p","name":"Livinus Paelinck","dates":"11 Oct 1718 Destelbergen – 1 Dec 1784 Destelbergen","confidence":"sup","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"11 Oct 1718 Destelbergen","order":"1718-10-11","died":"1 Dec 1784 Destelbergen","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","father":"adrianus_p","mother":"livina_pickaut","spouses":[{"id":"petronilla_vk","name":"Petronilla Carolina Van Kerckhove","detail":"Kalken, 7 Nov 1739"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Married in Kalken, his wife's home village; lived in Destelbergen."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"livinus_bundervoet","name":"Livinus Bundervoet","dates":"~1600 – ~1651","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"~1600","order":"1600","died":"~1651","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"petrus_bundervoet1560","spouses":[{"id":"elisabeth_nn","name":"Elisabeth NN","detail":"1st — mother of Segerius"},{"name":"Catharina van Hecke","detail":"2nd — mother of Wilhelmina; no record of her own yet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Of Evergem; married twice. His son Segerius (~1615), through whom our line descends,\nwas by his first wife.\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026), on two points, both against the tree this record already cited.\n\n**The surname \"Hovelynck\" is withdrawn.** This record called Segerius's mother\n\"Elisabeth Hovelynck\" and attributed that to the paulderidder tree. That tree records\nher as \"Elisabeth NN\" — a given name and nothing else. Where \"Hovelynck\" came from is\nnot known; it is in no source reachable from here, so it has been removed rather than\nrepeated. She now has her own record as [[elisabeth_nn]], deliberately without a surname.\n\n**The order of the marriages was the wrong way round.** The record had Catharina van\nHecke first and Elisabeth second. The children date it the other way: Elisabeth's son\nSegerius was born about 1615, while Catharina van Hecke (~1620–~1670) is shown in\npaulderidder under \"half-siblings\" as the mother of Wilhelmina Bundervoet (~1650).\nA wife born about 1620 cannot be the earlier marriage of a man whose son arrived in\n1615. Elisabeth is therefore first, Catharina second.\n\nCatharina van Hecke has no record of her own yet, nor does her daughter Wilhelmina —\nboth are blood relatives and belong in the tree. See also the note on [[willem_vanhecke]]\nabout two van Hecke women marrying into consecutive generations of this family."});
