FamilyTree.person({"id":"louise_bocklandt","name":"Louise Marie Bocklandt","dates":"31 Dec 1877 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) – 1946 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"31 Dec 1877 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1877-12-31","died":"1946 Oostende","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","father":"edouard_bocklandt","mother":"marie_vanbergen","spouses":[{"id":"edouard_dk","name":"Édouard Dekeyser","detail":"m. 4 May 1901 (likely Oostende); divorced ~1923"}],"source":"wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Rijksarchief AGATHA (parents on her record); Geneanet tree wete1998 (Erik Bekaert); Édouard's 1946 marriage act (records their divorce)\n\nBorn 31 Dec 1877 in Hamme (OOST-VLAANDEREN, Waasland) — the SAME town as her husband Édouard Dekeyser (both Hamme natives who moved to Oostende). This is the true source of the long 'Hamme' confusion: it was the couple's shared birth-town, not Hamme-Merchtem and not a marriage place. Married Édouard 4 May 1901 (the marriage legitimized their two eldest children); they later DIVORCED (~1923, decree Rechtbank van eersten aanleg Brugge — per Édouard's 1946 remarriage act). Died 1946 Oostende, buried at Stene. Her Bocklandt family is a Hamme (O-Vl) / Waasland family documented back to the 1760s (see her parents and the Bocklandt / Van Bergen ancestors)."});
