FamilyTree.person({"id":"morree","name":"Anna Francisca Morree","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Morree","family":"morree","branch":"Devriendt","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"francl_s","name":"Franciscus Leopoldus Smessaert"}],"source":"Marriage act — Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert × Anna Francisca Morbeé, Brugge, 16 August 1851","note":"STRONG LEAD, NOT GRAFTED (July 2026) — see [[francl_s]] for the whole of it. A Brugge\nmarriage act of 1851 gives an Anna Francisca **Morbeé**, daughter of Petrus Josephus Morbeé\nand Joanna De Clerck, marrying a Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert. The forenames and the\nhusband match; the surname does not.\n\nMorree and Morbeé are a plausible pair to confuse in a nineteenth-century hand — the double\nr and the rb are near-identical in cursive — and this record's spelling comes from a member\ntree, not from an act. That makes the act the better authority in principle, but \"in\nprinciple\" is not evidence, so nothing is changed here. Her son's 1857 Oostende birth act\nwould settle which spelling the registrar used."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"mtheresia_vandenbroeck","name":"Maria Theresia Van den Broeck","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van den Broeck","family":"vandenbroeck","died":"","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"desiderius_dk","name":"Desiderius De Keyser"}],"source":"Édouard Dekeyser's 1946 Oostende remarriage act (akte nr. 81); FamilySearch","note":"Source detail: Oostende marriage act nr. 81, 9 May 1946 (FamilySearch, Belgium West Flanders Civil Registration 1582-1950 — image read directly), naming her as mother of Eduardus De Keyser\n\nMOTHER of Édouard Dekeyser. Named in Édouard's 1946 remarriage act as his mother, 'overleden' (deceased) by then. Van den Broeck is a Waasland / Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) name, consistent with the family's Hamme origin. Frontier: her dates/parents, in the Hamme (O.-Vl.) registers."});
