FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_b1727","name":"Petrus (Pieter) Bundervoet","dates":"~1727 Evergem – 1777","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"~1727 Evergem","order":"1727","died":"1777","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"joannes_b","mother":"livina_stockman","spouses":[{"name":"Marie Anna de Deckere","detail":"m. ~1750 — she has no record of her own yet"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Younger son of Joannes Bundervoet (~1682–1760) and Livina Stockman, and the brother of\nChristoffel (1709–1786) through whom our line descends. He existed in this tree only as\nthe string \"Pieter (1727)\" inside his father's note; every person referenced anywhere is\nsupposed to have their own record, and now he does.\n\nThe death is recorded as a burial, not a death: paulderidder gives \"deceased, aged about\n50\" with a burial at Assenede on 13 December 1777, and no date of death. The year is\nsafe, the day is the burial's, and the two are kept apart rather than collapsed into a\ndeath date the source never gave. Assenede, a little north of Evergem, is also the first\nsign of this branch moving off the home parish.\n\nFRONTIER — his family, eight children strong, none of them yet recorded here. From\npaulderidder: married about 1750 to Marie Anna de Deckere (~1731–1809), with Joannis\n(1751), Livinus (1752), Petronella (1754–1794), Christophorus (1755), Joannis Baptista\n(1757), Livina Maria (1760–1831), Joanna (1761–1825) and Coleta (1766–1807). They are\nblood relatives of Renée and Léon — a great-uncle's whole household — and belong in the\ntree under objective 2. They are listed here rather than grafted because this pass took\nthe direct ancestors first, as the charter's priority requires.\n\nA second document sits on his paulderidder profile, captioned \"Petrus Bundervoet Akte\nvan teraardebestelling\" — a burial act. Not yet retrieved."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_bundervoet1560","name":"Petrus Bundervoet","dates":"1560 – ~1605","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"1560","order":"1560","died":"~1605","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"name":"NN Vyveraert"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"The earliest documented ancestor of the Bundervoet line (Evergem, ~1560); married twice and was the father of Livinus.\n\nCORRECTION (July 2026) to the note recorded a pass earlier. The full-text find was written\nup from search snippets as \"a Catherine Bundervoet widowed at Meirelbeke in 1587\" and a fief\nchain of 1687-1700. Reading the actual page ([[bundervoet-fiefs-alost-1687-1701]]) shows the\nsnippets had merged two adjacent entries: the Meirelbeke 1587 one belongs to the surname VAN\nDEN BUNDERE, not Bundervoet.\n\nWhat the page does show is a Bundervoet family at **Saint-Pierre-Alost**, holding fiefs from\n**1687 to 1701** — Catherine as widow and guardian in 1687, then Liévin son of François and\nLiévin son of Pasquier in 1700, and Pasquier son of Liévin in 1701. Descent stated, in the\nright century, some 30 km from Evergem. A lead for objective 3, and still not a link."});
