FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_f","name":"Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet","dates":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem – 21 Jul 1943 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem","order":"1879-03-19","died":"21 Jul 1943 Oostende","occupation":"werkman / meestergast","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"bernardus","mother":"goethals","spouses":[{"id":"augusta","name":"Augusta Vanstechelman"}],"source":"Doodsprentjes.be memorial card — Pieter Franciscus Bundervoet, d. Oostende 21 July 1943; Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Pieter-Franciscus Bundervoet, d. Oostende 21 July 1943; Geneanet","note":"The FIRST of the Bundervoet line to leave Evergem for the coast: born in Evergem, he settled in Oostende, where all his children were born from 1905 onward. Married Augusta Vanstechelman (the Bundervoet–Vanstechelman junction). FRONTIER (MyHeritage, July 2026): two independent Bundervoet family trees on MyHeritage — one run by Lucien Bundervoet, one by Johny Henricus Bundervoet, both in Belgium — agree that he and Augusta had SIX children, not the one recorded here: Alphons Bernardus Cyprianus, Emilius Josephus, Achilles, Henricus Eduardus, Irena Augusta and Camillus Edmundus. The same trees give him at least four siblings, one named Maria Bundervoet. His own birth and death match ours exactly (19 Mar 1879 Evergem, 21 Jul 1943), which is what makes the match credible. NOT GRAFTED: member trees are not records and no dates for the children were readable, so the five siblings need their Oostende birth acts (1905 onward) before they go in.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026), and by two archives that do not share a source. Doodsprentjes.be\nand Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust each hold a memorial-card record for him, and both\ngive birth 19 March 1879 at Evergem, death 21 July 1943 at Oostende, and a Vanstechelman\npartner — the Familiekunde one naming her in full as Augusta. Four identifiers agreeing\nacross two independent collections, where before this record rested on a Geneanet tree.\n\nConfidence stays `sup` rather than rising to `doc`: these are transcriptions of memorial\ncards. The Doodsprentjes scan is behind a session — the record's image URL returns the\nsite's search page, not the card — so no image has been read here. Reading it, or the\nOostende 1943 civil death act, is what would make this `doc`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_jos_keirsebilck","name":"Petrus Josephus Keirsebilck","dates":"13 Oct 1764 Oostkamp – 20 May 1817 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"Keirsebilck","family":"keirsebilck","born":"13 Oct 1764 Oostkamp","order":"1764-10-13","died":"20 May 1817 Oostkamp","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"joannes_keirsebilck_1728","mother":"maria_c_declerck","spouses":[{"id":"anna_fr_degrande","name":"Anna Francisca De Grande","detail":"Oostkamp, 4 Oct 1785"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Father of Joanna Keirsebilck (1791). Parents Joannes Keirsebilck (1728-1781) x Maria Catharina De Clerck (1727-1768)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_sabbe","name":"Petrus Sabbe","dates":"d. 31 Dec 1652 Oostkamp (Ruddervoorde)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Sabbe","family":"sabbe","died":"31 Dec 1652 Oostkamp (Ruddervoorde)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"willem_sabbe_y","mother":"clara_vandeputte","spouses":[{"id":"judoca_vandenberghe","name":"Judoca Vandenberghe","detail":"Oostkamp, 11 Jun 1616"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw (Rijksarchief aktes; Sosa 6760)\n\nAlso 'Schabbe'. Married Judoca Vandenberghe 1616; nine children incl. Simon Sabbe (1627). Witness at the wedding was his uncle Michiel Sabbe (b.1557). Parents Willem Sabbe x Clara Vande Putte. The Sabbe line runs back to Judocus 'Joos' Sabbe (~1475) around Harelbeke."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_sabbe_1504","name":"Petrus Sabbe","dates":"1504 Zwevegem – 1557","confidence":"sup","surname":"Sabbe","family":"sabbe","born":"1504 Zwevegem","order":"1504","died":"1557","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"judocus_sabbe_1475","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Born 1504 in Zwevegem (reign of Charles V), a farmer. Father of Willem Sabbe (~1530). Son of Judocus 'Joos' Sabbe (~1475), grandson of Gillis Sabbe (~1440)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vandewalle","name":"Petrus Vandewalle","dates":"d. 1658","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","died":"1658","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"simon_vandewalle_1565","mother":"christina_desangere","spouses":[{"id":"francisca_vanhoutte","name":"Francisca Van Houtte (partner)"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Father of Carolus Vandewalle (1638, born out of wedlock to Francisca Van Houtte). Son of Simon Vandewalle, the sexton of Oostkamp."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vannieuwenhuyse","name":"Petrus Van Nieuwenhuyse","dates":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp – 1701","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Nieuwenhuyse","family":"vannieuwenhuyse","born":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp","order":"1649-03-07","died":"1701","occupation":"schepen van Oostkamp (alderman)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"marinus_vannieuwenhuyse","mother":"cornelia_govaert","spouses":[{"id":"jacoba_monballiu","name":"Jacoba Monballiu","detail":"Oostkamp, 23 Jul 1673"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw; birth act agatha.arch.be scan 513_9000_000_00774 (Sosa 3382)\n\nFather of Anna Van Nieuwenhuyse (1676). Served as a schepen (alderman/magistrate) of Oostkamp. Parents Marinus Van Nieuwenhuyse (~1620-1666) x Cornelia Govaert (~1625-1653)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vanrenterghem","name":"Petrus Van Renterghem","dates":"~1500 – before 1530","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Renterghem","family":"vanrenterghem","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"before 1530","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp area. Father of Guillielmus Van Renterghem (~1530). Top of this line; no parents recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_wittenheyns","name":"Petrus Wittenheyns","dates":"~1500 – before 1575","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"before 1575","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"judoca_tjonck","name":"Judoca 't Jonck"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp. Father of Barbara Wittenheyns (~1535). The Wittenheyns of Oostkamp appear on two independent lines of ours (also\n[[mattheus_wittenheyns]] ~1500, via the Vandewalle line); whether Petrus and Mattheus\nare brothers is not established. No parents recorded.\n\nCHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the duplicate detector flags Petrus and Mattheus as\npossibly one person, on a rare surname plus a birth year of about 1500. They are not.\nFour things separate them, and none is a spelling difference:\n\n- different given names — Mattheus and Petrus are not variants of one another;\n- different wives — Judoca 't Jonck here, Maria De Ruwe there;\n- different deaths — before 1575 here, about 1546 at Oostkamp there;\n- different children — Barbara (~1535) here; Mattheus's children are named with him in\n  the 1547 Bruges orphan register.\n\nTwo men of one uncommon surname, born about the same time in the same parish, is what a\npair of brothers or cousins looks like. The warning is expected to keep firing, because\nit is derived from surname and year alone; this note is the answer to it."});
