FamilyTree.person({"id":"simon_vandewalle_1565","name":"Simon Vandewalle","dates":"~1565 Oostkamp – 28 Jul 1636 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","born":"~1565 Oostkamp","order":"1565","died":"28 Jul 1636 Oostkamp","occupation":"koster / landman (church sexton / farmer)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"simon_vandewalle_1530","mother":"joanna_wittenheyns","spouses":[{"id":"christina_desangere","name":"Christina Desangere"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Sexton (koster) of Oostkamp church and a Bruges citizen; grave inscription survives in the church. In a 1635 deed he swore he was born in Oostkamp and was then 70 (=> b. ~1565). Extensive property records 1597-1621."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"simonne","name":"Simonne Vandewalle","dates":"b. 1913–1914 Oostende?","confidence":"fam","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","born":"1913–1914 Oostende?","order":"1913","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"gustaaf","name":"Gustaaf Dekeyser"}],"source":"Geneanet; The family itself","note":"Source detail: Family (confirmed maiden name). Oostende candidates: Simonne Florida Vandewalle 1913 & Simonne Augusta 1914 — West-Vlaanderen civil birth acts (Geneanet)\n\nRESEARCH NOTE. Vandewalle is one of the most common West-Flemish surnames, so isolating her needs a linking record. Two strong Oostende candidates of the right age: (a) Simonne Florida Vandewalle, b. 6 Jun 1913 Oostende — parents Petrus Franciscus Antonius Vandewalle (1884) & Magdalena Clementia Willaert (1888); grandparents Franciscus Eduardus Vandewalle × Mathildis Vandierendounck and Emilius Willaert (1856) × Maria Lauwereins (1856–1893); (b) Simonne Augusta Vandewalle, b. 1914 Oostende. Neither is yet tied to Gustaaf. Decisive record: the Gustaaf × Simonne marriage (Oostende ~1938–40, or England 1940–43) — it would name her parents — or Roland’s 1943 UK birth (mother’s maiden name).\n\nCHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HER (July 2026). Her best candidate scores 27 bits\nand is **Alice Marie Van de Walle**, who was bearing Dekeyser children at Mariakerke in 1904\nand 1907 — a decade before our Simonne was born. She is not a candidate at all.\n\nWhat made the score is worth understanding, because it will recur on this line: the\nagreement is \"surname Vandewalle\" plus \"child names\", and the child-name agreement amounts\nto *her children were surnamed Dekeyser too*. A Vandewalle woman with Dekeyser children is\nthe shape of our Simonne, but in West-Vlaanderen it is also the shape of a great many other\nwomen — Vandewalle and Dekeyser are both among the commonest surnames in the province. No\ndate and no place agreed. Nothing grafted.\n\nHer identity still turns on the record her own note names: the Gustaaf x Simonne marriage,\nor Roland's 1943 English birth certificate with the mother's maiden name."});
