FamilyTree.person({"id":"thiery_f","name":"François Thumas","dates":"b. 1930–1939","confidence":"fam","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"1930–1939","order":"1930","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jean_t","mother":"crabbe","spouses":[{"id":"juliette","name":"Juliette Vandenhoeck"}],"source":"The family itself","note":"Named by the family. His father is almost certainly Jean Thumas (1907–1995), who stayed in Kraainem — and Jean’s wife was Marie Louise Crabbé, so she is François’s mother. This father-link falls inside the 100-year privacy window and is the only remaining inference. Everything above it is documented: Jean → J.B. Georgius (1876) → Georges Carolus Josephus (1836) → the Grez-Doiceau Thumas trunk back to 1656."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden","name":"Joanna Vandenbemden","dates":"15 Jun 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 29 Apr 1948 Kraainem","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"15 Jun 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1882-06-15","died":"29 Apr 1948 Kraainem","occupation":"naaister (seamstress)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"hendrik_vdb","mother":"coekelberghs","spouses":[{"id":"jbgeorgius","name":"J.B. Georgius Thumas","detail":"Kraainem, 3 Feb 1902"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; jswaelens","note":"Source detail: Geneanet (jswaelens); her 1902 Kraainem marriage act\n\nA seamstress; married J.B. Georgius Thumas in Kraainem in 1902. Her parents are named in that marriage act. Several of her children died in infancy.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where she is the bride: born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\non 15 June 1882, living at Kraainem, *naaister* — the occupation already held here,\nconfirmed word for word — and daughter of Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden and Maria\nTheresia Coekelberghs."});
